title: Close view
pid: a9ae1f60-41f7-44e0-a5a7-c53f41c67720
body: |2-
    - Request: =((request . "close view") (view-id . "VIEW_ID"))=. Each
      client sends it when a buffer showing a view is killed ('skg-send-close-view'
      on Emacs's 'kill-buffer-hook'; 'send_close_view' on Neovim's
      BufDelete and BufWipeout), and waits for no answer.
    - Response: LP =((response-type close-view) (content "view closed"))=,
      or =(content "Error: missing view-id")= when the request names no
      view ('server/serve/handlers/close_view.rs').
    - The server forgets the view: its viewforest and viewnode IDs go,
      and no later save rerenders it. Closing the last open buffer of the
      diff view also drops the graph straddle, which the diff view's
      buffers share; the next diff view builds it anew.
